    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW266b2wAzfAJMBjD5JpGuLWE)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Independent; fixes the colour cycling added in #499 (already merged).\n\n## What changes\n\n- Your DEVONthink colour items have descriptions (\"Red - Important point\"), so the exact titles Yellow, Red, Green, Blue were never found.\n- `Caps+c` now searches the Format menu for an item whose title starts with the colour name.\n- Cycle order follows your menu: Red, Green, Blue, Yellow, Orange, Purple, Grey.\n- If a colour is missing, an alert names the colour instead of a full menu path.\n- Renaming a colour's description no longer breaks it; renaming its first word does.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [x] Reload Hammerspoon: no error in the console.\n- [x] In DEVONthink, Caps+`c` repeatedly: the alert shows Red, Green, Blue, Yellow, Orange, Purple, Grey, then Red again.\n- [x] Each press changes the checked colour in the Format menu.\n- [x] Select text in a PDF and press Caps+`c`: it highlights in the new colour.\n- [x] If \"No colour starting with ...\" appears, tell me the Format menu path of the colour list.\n- [x] Caps+`x` still starts highlighting; both keys do nothing in other apps.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCTb5QFPFZUd9wzRgq)_",
